     1	# Reset experiment: plan (draft 1, 2026-11-09; not approved; no spend)
     2	
     3	**Why.** The round-9 fresh reviewer (problem 2, `docs/paper/external-review-r9.md`): the gain is excess profit when
     4	identity replacement is available; it does not show how much of that profit comes from the ability to replace an
     5	identity. The paper's premise is that free replacement makes a ban costless and that R3 removes that advantage. This
     6	plan measures the value of replacement directly.
     7	
     8	**Status.** Draft for internal review (Sol + Astra), then a decision card for the author. Nothing runs before the author
     9	approves the spend. This file is frozen (commit hash recorded in the ledger) before any paid cell starts.
    10	
    11	## 1. What already exists (free, seen before this plan)
    12	
    13	The D2+H3 family is D2 plus one binary knob `x` (`sim/policies/identity.py`: `x = 1` exits in the round after a failed
    14	audit and re-enters under a fresh identity; `x = 0` is plain D2). The second test registered D2 searches at the headline
    15	market only (design 8.1, "Matched core extras"). At `headline@rho0.2`, same 200 evaluation seeds, same frozen reference
    16	per rule (checked: `seeds` and reference `upstream` hashes equal):
    17	
    18	| Rule | g(D2+H3) | g(D2) | Replacement increment I = g(D2+H3) - g(D2) | Paired SE of I | D2+H3 flagged |
    19	|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
    20	| B2 | 0.5851 | 0.0027 | 0.5824 | 0.0011 | no |
    21	| B3 (F000) | 0.3502 | 0.0435 | 0.3067 | 0.0012 | yes |
    22	| R3 (F111) | 0.0486 | 0.0361 | 0.0124 | 0.0009 | yes |
    23	| C* | 0.0872 | 0.0433 | 0.0439 | 0.0008 | no |
    24	
    25	Source: `results/v2/eval/all/evaluate/headline@rho0.2__{rule}__{D2+H3,D2}__profit.json`, field `gain`; flags from
    26	`report.json` `search_flagged`. (At `headline@rho1`, R3 and C* are in the terminal-reserve collapse and I is 0.0025.)
    27	
    28	Reading: at the headline market, replacement accounts for about 88% of the attacker's gain against B3 and about a quarter
    29	against R3; the B3 - R3 gap is 0.302 with replacement and 0.007 without. These numbers are exploratory: they were seen
    30	before this plan, so the fresh-market part below is a replication on markets whose D2 results nobody has seen.
    31	
    32	## 2. Estimand and design (fresh markets)
    33	
    34	- **Estimand.** For rule r in {B3 (F000), R3 (F111), C*} and fresh market m: I(r, m) = mean over the 200 evaluation seeds
    35	  of g(D2+H3) - g(D2), both evaluated against the same frozen truthful reference of (r, m). Pooled: equal market weights.
    36	  Derived: the share of the B3 - R3 gap due to replacement, 1 - [g_B3(D2) - g_R3(D2)] / [g_B3(D2+H3) - g_R3(D2+H3)].
    37	- **New cells.** D2 x {F000, F111, C*} x fresh0..fresh5 at rho 0.2: **18 search cells**, each with the registered D2
    38	  search budget, the registered seeds (training seeds for search, the 200 evaluation seeds of the market for evaluation),
    39	  and the existing frozen references and D2+H3 records (no reference is re-selected; no D2+H3 cell is rerun).
    40	- **Doubling checks.** All 18 cells, as design 6.5 (doubled restarts; held-out evaluation of the doubled winner on the
    41	  same seeds); flags reported beside the estimates.
    42	- **Code.** The frozen second-test code at the protocol-v2 tag; only a new manifest lists the 18 cells. Any code change
    43	  is a deviation and is recorded.
    44	- **Not in scope (option B, priced below, not proposed by default).** An X7-SC variant with replacement disabled (`h_R = T`,
    45	  `lambda = 1`, other knobs searched): 18 more cells. It is a new family, so its result would be a new descriptive
    46	  analysis, not a replication of a registered cell.
    47	
    48	## 3. Analysis (fixed now)
    49	
    50	- Per market and pooled: I(r, m) with a paired nominal 95% interval over seeds (descriptive; the uncertainty is over seeds
    51	  only, conditional on the six markets and the frozen policies and references, as in the paper).
    52	- The contrasts I(B3) - I(R3) and I(C*) - I(R3), per market and pooled, and the derived share of the B3 - R3 gap.
    53	- The doubled-winner versions of the same quantities, as in the paper's `tab:ph-doubled`.
    54	- No confirmatory test, no multiplicity family, no change to any registered decision.
    55	
    56	## 4. Pre-specified expectations (written before any fresh D2 result exists)
    57	
    58	From the headline result in section 1 we expect, on each fresh market: I(B3) > I(R3); I(C*) > I(R3); and a pooled share of
    59	the B3 - R3 gap due to replacement of at least 0.5. Any of these failing is reported as a failed expectation in the
    60	paper, with the same weight as a success.
    61	
    62	## 5. What the paper would say
    63	
    64	- If the expectations hold: R3's advantage over B3 is mainly the removal of the replacement payoff, and C* leaves more
    65	  value in replacement than R3 does (a mechanism-level account the reviewer asked for).
    66	- If they fail: the gain differences come mostly from non-replacement behaviour (bidding, shading, allocation), and the
    67	  paper's framing must say so.
    68	- Either way, section 1's headline numbers are labelled exploratory, and the fresh result is labelled as a follow-up
    69	  analysis specified on 2026-11-09, after the round-9 review and after the headline D2 contrast was seen.
    70	
    71	## 6. Cost (estimate; the benchmark rule of design 8.2 applies)
    72	
    73	Units as design 8.2: one D2 cell = 1 unit + 0.16 for 200 evaluation seeds; a doubling check = 1 unit plus its held-out
    74	evaluation. Measured cost of the second test's evaluation: 39.45 USD for about 696 units = **0.057 USD per unit**
    75	(addendum; design 8.2 table).
    76	
    77	| Option | Units | USD at 0.057 | With 30% contingency |
    78	|---|---:|---:|---:|
    79	| A. D2 on 6 fresh markets (18 cells + 18 doubling checks) | about 39 | about 2.2 | **about 2.9** |
    80	| B. adds X7-SC with replacement disabled (18 cells x 2.5 x 1.16 + 18 checks x 2.5) | about 97 more | about 5.5 more | about 7.2 more |
    81	
    82	Pods: 16 vCPU at at most 0.56 USD per hour, the existing launchers and guards (snapshot, tarball, history, AppleDouble,
    83	`same_code`), one pod per market or one pod for all, deleted and verified after each run.
    84	
    85	**Caps and stop rules.** Option A cap 4 USD; option B cap 12 USD in total. Stop at the cap; a failed attempt counts
    86	toward it. No other paid work. Spend recorded in `docs/revision/budget-ledger.json` with a new reservation and in the
    87	operations ledger. The author's approval sentence is recorded verbatim before the first pod.
    88	
    89	## 7. Steps
    90	
    91	1. Internal review of this plan (Sol + Astra) to consensus; freeze it (commit).
    92	2. Decision card: option A (recommended), A + B, or no run.
    93	3. On approval: manifest for the 18 cells; a local dry run of one cell on 10 seeds (free); then the pods.
    94	4. Analysis: a new `reset` block in `posthoc_v2.py` (tested first), a new table, and a paragraph in section 9 of the paper
    95	   with sites; section 1's headline numbers enter at the same time, labelled exploratory.
    96	5. Internal review of the paper change, then the next external package.

