docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-22-revision-program-design.md:590:  share. Per-market and headline Q1 results are descriptive (the headline market was used in development).
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-22-revision-program-design.md:591:- **Q2, descriptive.** Per market and family, effect coding over the 8 cells: main effect of P = mean of the 4 cells with
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-22-revision-program-design.md:596:  reference terms and efficiency beside each contrast). Pooled over the 6 fresh markets as in 9.2. Nominal 95 percent
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-22-revision-program-design.md:598:- **Q3, descriptive.** Per core rule (F000, F111, C*), the attack envelope: the family among {D2+H3, X7-SC, X5-AG/v2,
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-22-revision-program-design.md:602:- **Q4, confirmatory on sampled markets.** Per fresh market, an intersection-union test: (a) H0: g_F000 - g_F111 <= 0.10
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-22-revision-program-design.md:603:  under D2+H3 and (b) H0: F111's gross efficiency <= 0.90, each one-sided; the market's p-value is the larger of the two
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-22-revision-program-design.md:604:  calibrated component p-values. A market passes if Holm across the 6 market p-values rejects it (one-sided tails 0.05/6 down to
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-22-revision-program-design.md:605:  0.05/1). Reported: k of 6 markets passing, and the markets. Wording: "replicated on k of 6 sampled markets"; failing
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-22-revision-program-design.md:606:  markets are named; "generalisation not established" when a market is not decided. No population claim.
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-22-revision-program-design.md:610:All claims are conditional on the six sampled markets, the stated neighbourhood, the fixed pair (Q1, Q2, Q4), the searched
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-22-revision-program-design.md:611:families, and the frozen searches. Q4 replicates the B3 - R3 comparison under D2+H3 and R3's efficiency condition, not the
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-22-revision-program-design.md:614:one. "Confirmatory" means specified before the fresh draw; it does not mean exact nominal error control on the fresh,
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-22-revision-program-design.md:615:selected-policy distributions (9.5). Q4 is an internal replication on fresh instances, not an independent-team
