### 6.4 References and freeze order

- **Menu.** A rule's truthful reference is selected on training seeds by the registered order (spec 5.2) from one menu:
  abstain, honest-max, and the twin, projection, and archive candidates of its D2+H3 and X7-SC searches. Every rule in the
  evaluation, including B2 and the rho = 1 repair cells, has exactly these two searches at the same budget (8.1), so
  matched pairs have equivalent menus. **Exception:** the secondary whole systems (B3-t, R3-t, C*-t) on fresh markets
  have no X7-SC cell (8.1); their fresh-market reference menu is abstain, honest-max, and the D2+H3 candidates, the same
  reduced menu for all three systems, and their fresh-market results are labelled accordingly. Its D2, X5-AG/v2, H4, and welfare gains use the same frozen reference; no other
  family adds candidates. Coalitions use their own joint reference (6.3).
- **Development reference** (tuning, comparator selection): the same construction with the tuning objective's families
  (D2, D2+H3, X7-SC) on the tuning markets. H4 is never available in development.
- **Dependency and freeze order per market.** (1) Profit attack and twin searches and banks; (2) reference selection and
  freeze; (3) the searches that need a frozen reference (W1) and the coalition steps 1 to 6 of 6.3 in their order; (4) envelope
  family choices (9.3 Q3), the fixed-attack bank and its training-seed matrix (6.6); (5) final freeze. Only then may any
  evaluation-seed episode of that market run; the evaluation stage refuses to run otherwise. Doubling results never enter
  the frozen candidates (6.5 says how they are used).

### 6.5 Search-quality checks

A doubling check continues the registered search with as many additional restarts as the registered budget (new restart
seeds), so the total budget doubles; it is reported as a diagnostic. Scheduled checks (fixed in the manifest):

- headline: the 10 matched rules (F000 to F111, C*, C*/S0) x {D2+H3, X7-SC} (20), the 12 welfare cells, and the 30
  coalition cells (24 X6-SE/v2, 6 X8-DB);
- fresh markets: the Q1 and Q4 rules (F000, F111, C*) x {D2+H3, X7-SC} x 6 (36).

98 checks. Units and threshold 0.005: gain (normalised by S*/N) for profit; G_tot and G_min (each normalised) for
coalitions; gross efficiency (a share of the first best) for welfare. Attack-profit and reference-profit changes are
reported separately. A W1 check that finds a feasible point where the original found none, or a feasible point with
efficiency lower by at least 0.005, labels the cell incomplete. Cells without a scheduled check (factorial cells on fresh
markets, whole systems, X5, H4, D2 extras) carry no search-quality claim.

**Two statuses.** A cell is **missing** if it did not run to completion or is invalid: not run (cap stop or cut), a
refused sample, a nonfinite statistic (9.2), a search with no finite candidate, or a failed load (H4). A cell is
**search-flagged** if it ran to completion but its scheduled doubling check exceeded the threshold above ("incomplete" in
the check's own wording). Consequences: a missing cell removes every confirmatory decision that uses it (the test is
reported "not decided: missing cell") and makes that part of its question unanswered (8.1a). A search-flagged cell keeps
its estimate as the estimate of the prescribed (frozen) search procedure; a confirmatory decision that uses it is still
made and is reported as a decision about the prescribed search procedure only; the robustness statement for that rule
and family (Q3) is reported unanswered ("search flagged"), never as "no attack found". **Held-out diagnostic:** for every scheduled check, the doubled search's winner (selected on its training
seeds) is evaluated unchanged on the cell's evaluation seeds against the same frozen reference, and reported beside the
cell; it never replaces or adds to the frozen estimate.

def _run_reference(item: dict, out: Path, cuts: int, h4_excluded: bool, catalog: list[dict]) -> str:
    rid = item["id"]; p = path_of(out, rid); old = read(p)
    if reusable(p, old, reference_provenance(item), lambda: check_record(rid, old, catalog, out, cuts, h4_excluded)):
        return "skipped"
    rec = stage_reference(item, out, cuts, h4_excluded); up = rec.pop("upstream")
    write(p, {"stage": "reference", "provenance": reference_provenance(item), "upstream": up, **rec})
    return "done"


def _run_one(stage: str, job: dict, out: str, cuts: int, h4_excluded: bool, catalog: list | None = None) -> str:
    out = Path(out); catalog = catalog or [job]
    if stage == "reference":
        return _run_reference(job, out, cuts, h4_excluded, catalog)
    if stage == "cross":
        return _run_cross(job, out, catalog)
    if stage in COALITION_STEPS:
        return coalition_step(stage, job, out, catalog)
    p = _stage_record_path(stage, job, out); rec = read(p)
    want = stage_upstream(stage, job, catalog, cuts, h4_excluded)
    def check():
        if set(rec.get("upstream") or {}) != want:
            raise ValueError("dependency set")
        validate(job, stage, rec, {u: path_of(out, u) for u in want})
        if stage == "evaluate":                                         # a damaged current record is recomputed, not skipped
            bad = _schema_problems(job, rec, len(job["mkt"]["seeds_eval"]))
            if bad:
                raise ValueError(bad)
        if stage == "doubling" and "heldout" not in rec:
            raise ValueError("doubling record without its held-out diagnostic")
    if reusable(p, rec, job["provenance"], check):
        return "skipped"
    body = {"search": stage_search, "dependent": stage_dependent, "evaluate": stage_evaluate}.get(stage)
    rec = body(job, out) if body else stage_doubling(job, out, cuts, h4_excluded)
    upstream = rec.pop("upstream", None)
    if stage in ("evaluate", "doubling") or upstream is None:
        upstream = {u: sha_file(path_of(out, u)) for u in sorted(want)}
    write(p, {"stage": stage, "id": job["id"], "provenance": job["provenance"], "upstream": upstream, **rec})
    return "done"


def _pool(stage, jobs, out, workers, cuts, h4_excluded, catalog=None) -> list:
def _waves(stage: str, jobs: list[dict], catalog: list[dict]) -> list[tuple[str, list]]:
    """The (stage, items) calls `run` makes, in order: priority tiers 0 to 3 (design 8.2), and inside a tier the dependency
    waves. Each call is a completion barrier: it returns only when all its items have finished."""
    out = []
    add = lambda st, items: out.append((st, items)) if items else None
    if stage == "search":
        for t in _tiers([j for j in jobs if j["objective"] in ("profit", "W0")]):
            add("search", [j for j in t if j["family"] != "X7-SC"]); add("search", [j for j in t if j["family"] == "X7-SC"])
    elif stage == "reference":
        for t in _tiers(_menu_items(jobs)):
            add("reference", t)
    elif stage == "dependent":
        for t in _tiers([j for j in jobs if j["objective"] in ("W1", "total", "min")]):
            add("dependent", [j for j in t if j["objective"] == "W1" and j["family"] != "X7-SC"])
            add("dependent", [j for j in t if j["objective"] == "W1" and j["family"] == "X7-SC"])
            co = [j for j in t if j["objective"] in ("total", "min")]; groups = {}
            for j in co:
                groups.setdefault((j["context"], _coalition_tag(j)), j)
            step = lambda kind, g, suffix="": {**g, "id": f"{kind}/{g['context']}/{_coalition_tag(g)}{suffix}", "record_id": f"{kind}/{g['context']}/{_coalition_tag(g)}{suffix}"}
            add("joint_twin", [step("joint_twin", g, f"_{s}") for g in groups.values() for s in _x6_schedules(_group(g, catalog))])
            add("dependent", [j for j in co if j["objective"] == "total"])
            add("joint_reference_pre", [step("joint_reference_pre", g) for g in groups.values()])
            add("dependent", [j for j in co if j["objective"] == "min"])
            add("joint_reference", [step("joint_reference", g) for g in groups.values()])
            add("coalition_select", [step("coalition_select", g) for g in groups.values()])
    elif stage == "evaluate":
        for t in _tiers(jobs):
            add("evaluate", t)
    elif stage == "cross":
        for t in _tiers(_cross_items(jobs)):
            add("cross", t)
    elif stage == "doubling":
        dbl = set(MAN.doublings())
        for t in _tiers([j for j in jobs if j["id"].replace(j["context"], manifest_ctx(j["context"]), 1) in dbl]):
            add("doubling", t)
    return out


def search_family(cell: Cell, family: Family, cache: SeedCache, st: SearchSettings, twin, extra_incumbents: dict | None = None):
    inc = {"twin_best": twin.best_knobs, "honest_point": family.honest_point(), **(extra_incumbents or {})}
    return cma_search(Objective(cell, family, cache), family, st, 1, incumbents=inc)


BOUNDED_CONTROLS = ("X7-SC", "H4")                # design draft 7, 5.2 and 5.3: Sobol corner controls, never every corner


def controls(objective, family: Family) -> list:
    if family.name in BOUNDED_CONTROLS:
        vecs = corner_vectors(family)
    else:
        if family.dim > 8:
            raise AssertionError(f"{family.name}: {family.dim} knobs is too many for exhaustive corners")
        vecs = family.corners()
    return [(k, float(objective.eval_knobs(k, source="corner"))) for k in vecs]


def continue_search(objective, family: Family, st: SearchSettings, original, seed: int = 1):
    """Doubling (design 6.5): as many new restarts as registered, with restart seeds after the registered ones, on the
    merged archive (old entries kept), the previous best as an incumbent."""
    objective.archive.update(original.archive)
    return cma_search(objective, family, st, int(seed) + int(st.restarts), incumbents={"previous_best": dict(original.best_knobs)})


